# RUN A REAL PAGE TWICE - ONCE COMPILED, ONCE INTERPRETED - AND COMPARE WHAT
# IT DREW. application.test does the same for a bare script::context; this
# drives the whole engine: examples/pages/invaders.html, its canvas, its sprite
# sheet and its requestAnimationFrame loop, with the compiled bodies installed
# through browser::set_script_prepared_hook (Runtime.cmake builds both arms).
#
# THE PIXELS ARE THE CONTROL AND THE COUNTERS ARE THE ASSERTION: both arms run
# the same game, so a page that installed nothing draws exactly the same
# picture. NO REAL FONTS: fillText goes through the text stack and two FreeType
# versions do not rasterise identically, so the bitmap font makes the picture
# the same on any machine and needs no font files.
#
# RUN: env CTBROWSER_FONTS=font8x8 CTBROWSER_NETWORK=0 ctcompile-test-launcher-page-vm %t.vm.ppm 2> %t.vm.err
# RUN: env CTBROWSER_FONTS=font8x8 CTBROWSER_NETWORK=0 ctcompile-test-launcher-page-aot %t.aot.ppm 2> %t.aot.err
# RUN: cmp %t.vm.ppm %t.aot.ppm
#
# A BLANK CANVAS WOULD ALSO MATCH: the page fills its background every frame,
# so two runs that drew nothing are two uniform colours that compare equal.
# The size says this is a 320x240 PPM rather than a truncated write; the
# colour count says something was drawn on it - three is the background, the
# sprites and the score text.
# RUN: test $(stat -c %%s %t.aot.ppm) -ge 230400
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=AOT < %t.aot.err
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VM < %t.vm.err
# AOT-DAG: colours = {{([3-9]|[1-9][0-9]+)$}}
#
# THE PAGE HAS FOUR FUNCTIONS AND ALL FOUR COMPILE: the top level, `frame`, and
# the two anonymous keydown/keyup listeners. install_strict refuses a partial
# install, so any other number is a page whose function count moved.
# AOT-DAG: installed 4 across {{[0-9]+}} script
#
# THE INTERPRETER MUST NEVER HAVE RUN. Unlike the bare-context arm this page is
# driven ENTIRELY from C++ - the top level once from load_html, then `frame`
# once per requestAnimationFrame - so C++ -> AOT is many (20 ticks plus the top
# level is 21 at least; not a pin, because a rAF callback the engine also
# invoked for another reason would be an engine change, not a fall back) and
# AOT -> AOT is zero: invaders' four functions never call one another, only
# natives - and a compiled body reaching ctx.drawImage, ctx.fillRect,
# Math.floor or requestAnimationFrame is an AOT -> C++ crossing, the mixed
# stack the plan's Definition of Done asks for by name. What must be zero is
# every path through the interpreter.
# AOT-DAG: transition "C++ -> VM" = 0{{$}}
# AOT-DAG: transition "VM -> AOT" = 0{{$}}
# AOT-DAG: transition "AOT -> VM" = 0{{$}}
# AOT-DAG: transition "C++ -> AOT" = {{(2[1-9]|[3-9][0-9]|[1-9][0-9][0-9]+)$}}
# AOT-DAG: transition "AOT -> C++" = {{[1-9][0-9]*}}
#
# THE BLINDED ARM, which must have run the frames too, or the comparison above
# is between two pages that did nothing.
# VM-DAG: transition "C++ -> AOT" = 0{{$}}
# VM-DAG: transition "VM -> AOT" = 0{{$}}
# VM-DAG: transition "AOT -> AOT" = 0{{$}}
# VM-DAG: transition "AOT -> VM" = 0{{$}}
# VM-DAG: transition "C++ -> VM" = {{(2[1-9]|[3-9][0-9]|[1-9][0-9][0-9]+)$}}
